{
    "about": "Shared cases of the links of a note (documentation/Canonical Form.md, section \"The links of a note\"). The TypeScript tests and the Rust tests read this file and must get what each case states. \"linkPaths\": a source text and the link paths that it must give, each one time, in the order of the code points. \"targets\": a list of the notes of a scan, and for a link path in the note \"from\" the vault path of its target, or null when it has none. \"links\": a source text with the notes of a vault and the ones that a guard excludes (\"ignored\"), and the list that the manifest entry must hold. Every name is invented, and every expected value is written by hand.",
    "linkPaths": [
        {
            "name": "a wikilink, and a wikilink with a link text",
            "text": "See [[Alpha]] and [[Beta|the second one]].\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Beta"]
        },
        {
            "name": "a link to a heading and to a block has the path of its note, one time, and a link into the note itself has none",
            "text": "[[Alpha#Part one]] [[Alpha#^b1]] [[Alpha#Part one|part]] [[#Here]] [[#^here]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha"]
        },
        {
            "name": "an embed",
            "text": "![[Gamma]]\n\n![[Delta#Part]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Delta", "Gamma"]
        },
        {
            "name": "a link in a table: the backslash before the bar is not part of the target",
            "text": "| [[Alpha\\|a]] | [[Beta\\|b]] |\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Beta"]
        },
        {
            "name": "spaces and tabs at the two ends of the target are removed, and a space before the hash stays",
            "text": "[[  Alpha  |x]] [[\tBeta\t]] [[Gamma #part]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Beta", "Gamma "]
        },
        {
            "name": "the last opening before the first closing",
            "text": "[[[Alpha]]] [[one [[Beta]] ]] [[Gamma]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Beta", "Gamma"]
        },
        {
            "name": "a link is on one line",
            "text": "[[Alpha\n]] [[Beta\n",
            "linkPaths": []
        },
        {
            "name": "a link text can hold a bracket and a bar",
            "text": "[[Alpha|see [1] | more]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha"]
        },
        {
            "name": "links in the properties",
            "text": "---\nrelated: \"[[Alpha]]\"\nsources:\n  - \"[[Folder/Beta|B]]\"\n  - '[[Gamma]]'\nurl: \"[site](Delta.md)\"\n---\nText\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Delta.md", "Folder/Beta", "Gamma"]
        },
        {
            "name": "the tool does not read Markdown: a link in code and in a comment is read too",
            "text": "`[[Alpha]]`\n\n```\n[[Beta]]\n```\n\n%% [[Gamma]] %%\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Beta", "Gamma"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Markdown links",
            "text": "[a](Alpha.md) [b](Folder/Beta%20one.md) [c](<Gamma two.md>) [d](Delta.md \"a title\") [e](Round_(1).md) [f](  Spaced.md  )\n",
            "linkPaths": [
                "Alpha.md",
                "Delta.md",
                "Folder/Beta one.md",
                "Gamma two.md",
                "Round_(1).md",
                "Spaced.md"
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "a Markdown link to a heading, and a destination that the line ends",
            "text": "[a](Alpha.md#part%20one) [b](<Gamma two.md#part>) [c](Beta.md\n[d](<Delta.md\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha.md", "Beta.md", "Gamma two.md"]
        },
        {
            "name": "a destination with a scheme, a destination into the note itself and an empty one are not read",
            "text": "[a](https://example.org/Alpha.md) [b](mailto:someone@example.org) [c](#part) [d]() [e](<>) [f](obsidian://open?file=Alpha)\n",
            "linkPaths": []
        },
        {
            "name": "the decoding of a destination",
            "text": "[a](caf%C3%A9.md) [b](a%26b.md) [c](bad%ZZ.md) [d](bad%C3.md) [e](%F0%9F%8C%B1%20Seedlings.md) [f](half%.md)\n",
            "linkPaths": [
                "a%26b.md",
                "bad%C3.md",
                "bad%ZZ.md",
                "café.md",
                "half%.md",
                "🌱 Seedlings.md"
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "the decoding refuses bytes that are not UTF-8, and keeps a byte order mark inside a name as a character",
            "text": "[a](long%C0%AFform.md) [b](half%ED%A0%80pair.md) [c](high%F4%90%80%80.md) [d](a%EF%BB%BFmark.md) [e](small%c3%a9.md)\n",
            "linkPaths": [
                "a\uFEFFmark.md",
                "half%ED%A0%80pair.md",
                "high%F4%90%80%80.md",
                "long%C0%AFform.md",
                "smallé.md"
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "a no-break space of a link is a space, as in Obsidian",
            "text": "[[Alpha\u00a0one]] [[\u00a0Beta\u00a0|x]] [c](Gamma%C2%A0two.md) [d](<Delta\u00a0two.md>) [e](%20Epsilon.md%20)\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha one", "Beta", "Delta two.md", "Epsilon.md", "Gamma two.md"]
        },
        {
            "name": "the white space at the two ends of a link is removed as Obsidian does: a hair space, a wide space and a byte order mark are white space, and the next line character (U+0085) is not",
            "text": "[[Alpha\u200a]] [[\u3000Beta\ufeff|x]] [c](Gamma.md%E2%80%8A) [[Delta\u0085]] [[Eps\u200ailon]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Alpha", "Beta", "Delta\u0085", "Eps\u200ailon", "Gamma.md"]
        },
        {
            "name": "the order of the code points, not of the UTF-16 units",
            "text": "[[🌱 Seedlings]] [[～ Pond]] [[Zinnia]] [[apple]]\n",
            "linkPaths": ["Zinnia", "apple", "～ Pond", "🌱 Seedlings"]
        }
    ],
